shape theory.physics.chirality : theory.physics.su2, theory.physics.energy, theory.physics.higgs {
  type: theorem
  layer: 0
  """
// Chirality Is Mass (02b §2.3).
// Chirality (handedness in SU(2)-complex) is what makes bound
// energy into mass.
//
// Energy without chirality: propagating (photons) or bound (gluons).
//   Massless.
// Energy with chirality: mass. Can be at rest. Has inertia.
//
// Chirality provides a loop to cycle around in SU(2) gauge space.
// Cycling things have moment of inertia. Moment of inertia resists
// changes to rotation. This resistance IS inertia. This IS mass.
//
// No loop -> no moment of inertia -> no mass -> must propagate at c.
//
// Local chirality: closes within one Planck shape. Full mass.
//   (leptons, quarks, W/Z, Higgs)
// Distributed chirality: closes across multiple Planck shapes.
//   Tiny mass. (neutrinos: XY -> YZ -> ZX while propagating)
//
// Gravitational mass = inertial mass: same chirality, different
// view. Inertial = chirality's resistance to change (internal).
// Gravitational = chirality's effect on spacetime (external).
// Equivalence principle is an identity, not a coincidence.
//
// E = mc^2: conversion between chiral (massive) and non-chiral
// (massless) structure. At Planck scale c=1, so E=m.
//
// Derives from: theory.physics.su2, theory.physics.energy,
//               theory.physics.higgs
  """
}
